course: dictionary
lesson: 13030
title: Faintness: dizzy or barely there
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Faintness is a noun, the name for the quality of being faint. «The hot bus made Sam feel a sudden faintness, so he sat down quickly.» Sat down and hot bus are the clues: faintness here is a dizzy, weak feeling, as if you might pass out.
explain: The second meaning is about things that are very weak. «The faintness of the candle made the dark room hard to see.» The candle is not making you feel dizzy. It means the light is so dim that it is hard to see by. The clues are candle, dark and hard to see.
explain: Ask yourself: is someone feeling dizzy, or is something weak and hard to see, hear or smell? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Faintness is a noun, which is a word for a thing you can feel or notice.
fact: Faintness can mean a weak, dizzy feeling, as if you might faint (pass out).
fact: Faintness can also mean being hard to see, hear or smell because it is very weak.
fact: «A feeling of faintness» means you feel dizzy and weak.
fact: First aid tip: if someone has a feeling of faintness, help them sit or lie down and raise their legs.
exercise: «After running in the hot sun, Mia felt a sudden faintness and had to sit down.» What does faintness mean here? | A loud, happy shout | A bright, shining light | *A weak, dizzy feeling
exercise: «The faintness of the candle made the dark room hard to see.» What does faintness describe? | *The weak, dim light of the candle | The strong heat of a fire | A loud noise from the street
exercise: Which sentence uses faintness to mean a dizzy feeling in the body? | «The faintness of the distant bird song was lovely.» | *«Ben felt faintness after he stood still in the sun too long.» | «The faintness of the stars made the sky look grey.»
test: «The faintness of the sound meant the radio was almost off.» What does faintness mean? | *Very weak, so hard to hear | Dizzy and sick | Loud and clear
test: Your friend says, «I have a feeling of faintness.» What should you do first? | *Help them sit or lie down and raise their legs | Run around and shout for a drink | Tell them to stand up quickly and walk away
exam: «The sudden faintness made Lily grab the chair, and she felt she might pass out.» What does faintness mean? | *A weak, dizzy feeling | A bright light | Being very hungry | Being very loud
